--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT SHIPPED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI TripPlannerPage at web parity: a pure @Observable state holder
(ADR-004 — no networking in the view) over an injectable TripPlannerDataSource seam whose primary
method keeps the web hook name at the Swift call site (planTrip ← usePlanTrip / POST /trip-planner/plan;
loadVehicles ← useSelectedVehicle / GET /vehicles; sendToCar ← POST /vehicles/{id}/command). The web
mutation lifecycle (idle → planning → loaded/failed) is modelled as TripPlanPhase and surfaced as the
three data states. The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer title + subtitle + the global
VehicleSelect) and every page-unit panel, each with its own state:

  GlassPanel1  — the "Plan Your Trip" form (origin/destination address fields, current + min-arrival
                 SOC sliders, driving-speed select, Plan-Trip + Send-to-Car actions, the vehicle-battery
                 readout). The rich address autocomplete is the sibling AddressInput parity unit; here
                 the HIG-native text fields capture the address the planner resolves.
  StatCards    — Distance / Total-Time / Driving / Charging / Energy / Est-Cost (the web 6-card grid),
                 each formatting SI at the boundary via TripPlannerFormat.
  GlassPanel8  — the Weather-Impact panel (shown on the web condition efficiency_factor !== 1.0).
  + the straight-line estimate disclaimer (route.is_estimate) and the not-feasible warning
    (!route.feasible), realized as HIG TSAlertBanners.

The custom web formatDuration h/m helper, fmtNumber grouping, formatCurrency (symbol + grouped number),
the formatEnergy({precision:1}) call, and the SI distance conversion are ported verbatim into the pure,
harness-verified TripPlannerFormat; SI→display conversion runs through the shared KMP Units facade
(P1/S5) at the render boundary only (ADR-005). TripLocation/TripPlanRoute/TripLeg/TripChargeStop/
TripWeatherImpact/TripSOCPoint/TripPlan mirror the /trip-planner/plan response shape; the page surfaces
route + weatherImpact, while legs/chargeStops/socCurve are carried for fidelity and consumed by the
sibling map / SOC-chart / leg-list parity units (resolvedDestination = legs.last.to powers Send-to-Car).

Adaptive (ADR-002/006): the address grid, the SOC/speed control grid, and the stat-card grid reflow for
macOS / iPad regular width vs. compact iPhone. The page is registered for the new `.tripPlanner` AppRoute
(web /trip-planner resolves to it directly via the canonical path segment "trip-planner"; grouped under
.vehicle alongside .driving / .efficiency) and hosted through TripPlannerRouteRegistration in
TeslaSyncApp. All 30 visible strings resolve from Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; the two
parameterized strings (form.vehicleBattery %lld, weather.factor %@) keep the exact web key + format via
String(format: String(localized:)). SI units render via Units + TripPlannerFormat at the boundary.

